{# "Popular flights near you" -- C12 (#401). The cheapest direct fare into
   each reachable city from the visitor's own suggested origin, split into
   domestic and international tabs.

   Renders through `place/fares.html.twig` unchanged -- the same tabset the
   city and country pages already use for their own "cheapest way in"
   block, just with the origin held fixed and the split on the destination
   side instead. `popular` is already the whole answer HomeController
   computed; a tab it dropped (usually international, from an origin whose
   country sells nowhere else) simply is not in the list.

   Silent when there is nothing to show, same as `index/deals.html.twig`. #}
{% if popular is not empty %}
    {# `.band-raised` on this outer div, full-bleed, and `.container` on the
       one inside it -- Bootstrap's container has its own max-width, so a
       background painted on it stops at that width rather than filling the
       viewport (C21, #422). #}
    <div class="band-raised" id="popular-flights">
        <div class="container px-4 py-5">
            <h2 class="pb-2 mb-4 border-bottom">Popular flights near you</h2>

            {% include 'place/fares.html.twig' with {'fares': popular} only %}
        </div>
    </div>
{% endif %}
